  designNotes: '2026-09-02, Meshy AI attack (跳躍頭部剪刀腳摔.zip / Jumping_Head_Scissor_Takedown,
    take "Scene", 3.67s) imported as Wushi_ScissorTakedown. Measured offline on the
    live 4x 武士: a LEAPING command-grab. hips localZ (forward) travels 0 -> ~10 units
    by nt 0.80 (then the clip drifts on to ~14.5 by nt 1.0 - the usual Meshy "starts
    behind root, walks forward" tail). hips localY jumps 1.7 -> 4.2 (nt 0.25, airborne)
    -> bottoms 0.69 (nt 0.70, the slam), feet leave the ground nt 0.15-0.55. Scissor
    the head in the air nt 0.30-0.50, drive down nt 0.50-0.70. Hit window nt 0.50-0.72
    (the takedown impact). deflectReaction ContinueCombo (追加94 續 44 - 武士 has no
    flinch clip). knockback 0 / launchesTarget 0 per user rule "only the kick knocks
    the player back".

    2026-09-02 續 46 - ENABLED. Clip re-imported lockRootPositionXZ (the ~10-unit baked
    forward travel stripped, jump height kept). Horizontal leap driven by the FSM:
    lungeDistanceFromTargetGap=1 replaces attackMotion.forwardDistance at commit with
    (live gap to player - lungeTargetGapMeters 1.4), clamped 0..7m, spent over
    attackMotion window nt 0.05-0.55 - lands ~1.4m in front of the player at any range,
    no BossAnimatorRootMotionRelay / applyRootMotion needed on 武士.
    NEEDS PLAY TUNING: lungeTargetGapMeters, the nt 0.05-0.55 window vs the visible jump
    arc, and whether the in-place jump reads OK with the root planted (feet leave via
    bone anim only). selectionWeight 0.5/0.6, 7s cooldown, minDistance 2 maxDistance 7.'
